# Provenance for the three per-product Starfleet OpenAPI specs in
# this directory: byoc.yaml, managed.yaml, account.yaml.
# control-plane.json has entirely different provenance, recorded in
# its own section at the BOTTOM of this file.
#
# These three are CAPTURED from the published public contracts, which
# the API serves unauthenticated:
#
#   GET https://api.pgedge.com/{account,byoc,managed}/v1/openapi.json
#
# Each is already filtered to the public, enterprise-maximal surface
# by the API's own public filter on the way out — enterprise is the
# union of what any tenant can be served, one CLI binary serves every
# tenant, and a verb outside the caller's plan fails with the API's
# own entitlement error. So the capture IS the public contract;
# nothing on this side derives or filters.
#
# RE-CAPTURE
#
#   make vendor-spec          # capture from production
#   make vendor-spec-check    # fetch and report drift, write nothing
#   make generate             # regenerate the three clients
#
# Then state anything that changed shape in the commit message.
# Capture only what production serves.
# Never hand-edit a captured spec.
#
# THE CAPTURE IS STILL FAIL-CLOSED, in the tool (cmd/vendorspec):
# every product is validated before any file is written, and the run
# aborts on an `x-pgedge-*` key anywhere in a contract (the upstream
# filter should have removed every marker, so one appearing means
# that filter regressed — do not vendor the regression), on
# `x-go-type-import` (it names an API-internal package this module
# cannot import, so the generated client would not compile; a bare
# `x-go-type` is expected — it names UUID, which each module's
# api/types.go supplies), and on a path outside the product's own
# namespace. TestVendoredSpecsCarryNoVisibilityMarkers and
# TestVendoredSpecsAreCanonical assert the first and third invariants
# over the committed artefacts too, so a hand edit cannot reintroduce
# either.
#
# The conversion to YAML is the only transformation: yaml.v3 parses
# the served JSON (integers survive as integers), and the encoder
# emits sorted keys at two-space indent, so two captures of the same
# contract are byte-identical regardless of served key order.
#
# WHAT IS DELIBERATELY ABSENT
#
#   * POST /account/v1/invites/{id}/accept — dropped by the API's own
#     public filter (x-pgedge-omit-public upstream). That costs
#     nothing: `starfleet invite accept` cannot work from an API client
#     under any circumstances — the API's edge proxy never sets both an
#     X-User-ID and an X-Client-ID — so the verb refuses locally with
#     exit 5. TestVendoredSpecsOmitPrivateOperations pins it.
#   * /billing/v1 — the API publishes no billing spec at all.
#     Deliberately GUI-only.
#
# =====================================================================
# CONTROL PLANE (control-plane.json)
#
# A different product with its own release cadence; nothing above
# applies to it. The spec is Goa-generated inside the control-plane
# repo and vendored VERBATIM — no filter, no derivation, no
# x-pgedge-* markers exist in it. `make vendor-spec` and
# `make vendor-spec-check` do NOT cover this file.
#
# scripts/cp-service-keys.sh and the cp-floor gate parse `^CP_TAG=`
# from this file, so this section keeps its CP_-prefixed names.
#
CP_REPO=https://github.com/pgEdge/control-plane
CP_TAG=v0.10.0
CP_SPECPATH=api/apiv1/gen/http/openapi3.json
#
# Vendor from RELEASED TAGS ONLY. The CLI supports Control Plane
# >= 0.10.0 (decision 2026-08-05); a dev snapshot's info.version
# lies about what routes it carries — the previous copy claimed
# v0.9.0 while carrying post-v0.9.0 routes.
#
# Re-vendor:
#   Step 0: internal/cp/svccfg is a hand-written mirror of
#     CP's per-service-type config key sets (mcp/rag/postgrest), pinned
#     to this same CP_TAG via svccfg.KeysFloor. It is NOT covered by
#     `make vendor-spec` or `make generate` -- reconcile it BEFORE
#     bumping CP_TAG below:
#       scripts/cp-service-keys.sh <control-plane checkout>
#     Fix any reported drift in internal/cp/svccfg (re-reading the
#     three source files at the NEW tag -- see that package's doc
#     comment), then bump svccfg.KeysFloor to match.
#   git -C <control-plane checkout> fetch --tags
#   git -C <control-plane checkout> show \
#     ${CP_TAG}:${CP_SPECPATH} > openapi/control-plane.json
#   make generate    # regenerates internal/cp/api
#
# The OpenAPI 3.0.3 document is openapi3.json; its Swagger 2.0
# sibling openapi.json is NOT the file to vendor.
# =====================================================================
